        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177-a1-a3">

                <pb facs="0315" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg273"/>

                <head>[Memorandum.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 27, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Mr. Kennard wishes you to send out 500
                    mechanics. He will have work for them, and more. Wages here—say, blacksmiths, $2
                    to $2 50 ; riveters, $1 50 to $2 ; fitters, the same; moulders, $1 50 ; and
                    trimmers, do., per day. Riveters wanted particularly. He also would like you to
                    send out 3,000 laborers. Their wages will be $1 25 per day. They should pay
                    their own way out. Mechanics can be had in Belfast and Scotland.</p>
                <p>Truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>McANDREW &amp; WANN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Henry</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
